	abstract = {Current disassembly enterprises exhibit imbalanced production line planning, significant susceptibility to external interference factors, and low disassembly efficiency. To improve the efficiency and stability of disassembly lines, this study incorporates industrial robots into traditional fully manual disassembly lines and proposes a fuzzy human-robot collaborative disassembly line balancing problem considering sequence-dependent setup time, introducing safety probability constraints to simultaneously reduce operational risks and enhance disassembly line efficiency. For solving the model, a hybrid simulated annealing algorithm was designed with a dual-layer encoding strategy and corresponding decoding method tailored to the problem characteristics. The hybrid simulated annealing algorithm was applied to a practical range hood disassembly line case and demonstrated superiority through comparative verification with five optimization algorithms. © 2025 IEEE.},
