	abstract = {This paper analyzes the dynamic disassembly line balancing problem based on product state uncertainty and regards it as a dynamic multi-objective optimization problem to solve. In dynamic multi-objective optimization problems, it is important to quickly track the Pareto optimal set and respond quickly to the changing environment. Domain generalization has been proved to have good adaptive ability for different environments. Therefore, this paper proposes an ensembled classifier algorithm based on domain generalization to deal with the dynamic disassembly line balancing problem. The algorithm uses the technique of domain generalization to train an ensembled classifier before the arrival of a new environment by using historical environment knowledge. The performance of the algorithm is improved by generating high-quality initial populations. Finally, based on a set of problem examples of different sizes and environmental similarities generated in this paper, and by comparing this algorithm with several latest comparative algorithms, the effectiveness of the algorithm is verified for the dynamic disassembly line balancing problem. © 2023 IEEE.},
